/// emptiness test, a non-null `None`, a head at the wrong index/scale/base, a
/// swapped tail-length subtraction, or a `Select` on the wrong field) FAILS THE
/// COMPILE CLOSED. Like `SplitAtRefinementJob` this is a VALUE-level (not
/// memory-op-sequence) obligation, so it lives in its own sink and drain.
